      "content": "# Initial Data Privacy Compliance Audit Report: Detailed Assessment\n\n## I. Introduction and Audit Scope\nThis report provides a granular assessment against the recently implemented data privacy mandates. Further decomposition allows for a more comprehensive mapping of controls.\n\n### I.A. Audit Objectives Defined\nThe primary goal is to verify adherence to new PII handling standards.\n\n## II. Data Security Requirements Review\nThis section focuses on the technical safeguards protecting sensitive data.\n\n### II.A. Encryption Standards Compliance (Requirement 1.1)\nVerification covers the implementation status of AES-256 or higher encryption for all data stored at rest.\n\n### II.B. PII Access Logging Mechanisms (Requirement 1.2)\nInspection addresses the logging procedures, ensuring capture of timestamp, user ID, and stated purpose for every access event.\n\n## III. Data Lifecycle Management Procedures\nThis area examines how long data is kept and how it is destroyed.\n\n### III.A. Data Retention Policy Definition (Requirement 2.1)\nWe assess the completeness of documented, explicitly defined retention periods across all datasets.\n\n### III.B. Automated Data Purging Implementation (Requirement 2.2)\nReview confirms the functionality of automated processes designed",
